cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use audioforge or its measurements, please cite it as below."
title: "audioforge: one frozen streaming encoder as a voice agent's speech front end"
abstract: >-
  A from-scratch PyTorch rebuild of the design shared by NVIDIA's audio models, and a study of whether one frozen
  115M cache-aware FastConformer with small heads (VAD, speaker, speaker-aware end of turn, target-speaker VAD) can
  serve a voice agent's streaming speech front end, measured task by task against dedicated models and end to end
  against the default local stacks of Pipecat and LiveKit.
authors:
  - family-names: Melichov
    given-names: Max
version: 0.1.0
license: Apache-2.0
repository-code: "https://github.com/maxmelichov/audioforge"
keywords:
  - speech recognition
  - voice activity detection
  - turn detection
  - speaker diarization
  - streaming
  - voice agents
